Option: clean-addresses-C
Name: Page addresses without .html (Cloudflare Pages)
Does: Sets PAGE_EXT = "" in tools/pages.py, so the extra pages name themselves to Google as /wise-pie, not /wise-pie.html (canonical tag, share address, structured data, sitemap). Cloudflare Pages redirects /wise-pie.html to /wise-pie, so without this the canonical tags point at an address that redirects. Updates the public-site test (a sitemap address may omit .html) and the README and checklist wording. Links inside the site keep .html.
Answers: d05 A (host: Cloudflare Pages), d38
Conflicts: none
Requires: none
Host: cloudflare
Order: 40
After: python3 tools/pages.py (the usual rebuild line is fine too); the 5 extra pages and sitemap.xml are rewritten
Strings: none

